{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":453,"recorded_at":1780531400000901,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c931-e80d-7592-9c45-0f3f325d0fe4"},"task_id":"01a0c931-e80d-7592-9c45-0f3f325d0fe4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c931-e80d-7592-9c45-0f3f325d0fe4","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/td8/results-rev7.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev7 — results (standalone)\n2|\n3|Ready for review. This run answers the rev6 CHANGES REQUESTED on\n4|checkpoint `d4bd91d0` (trunk unmoved, no rebase): the P1 and P2-A\n5|close as one invariant with its fact enumeration, P2-B closes\n6|with the composed effect-level witness, and P3 closes with the\n7|reclassification plus a genuinely admitting loop mutant. Every\n8|rev6 closure is retained (B43 handoff, ordering lock, refresh\n9|bound, importer corpus, corrected census). The worktree is\n10|intentionally UNCOMMITTED for the Story handoff snapshot.\n11|\n12|Scope of the production delta (all in `internal/tmuxserver`):\n13|`ops.go` (two post-lock attach rechecks plus the boundary\n14|comment). No other production file changed. Touched landed\n15|files: none (the cross-package harness row patches\n16|`terminalbackend/conformance.go` only inside its own run and\n17|restores it; the candidate tree holds no landed diff).\n18|\n19|## Finding-by-finding disposition\n20|\n21|| # | Verdict finding | Disposition | Witness |\n22||---|---|---|---|\n23|| P1 | generation admission goes stale while attach waits for its new lock (no generation recheck at the effect boundary) | FIXED — live `CurrentGeneration` recheck under the lock immediately before the receipt commit; same-Lifecycle rotation before lock acquisition now refuses | `TestAttachRefusesGenerationRotatedDuringLockWait` via `Lifecycle.Execute` (channel-ordered rotation, deterministic); narrowing `N-attach-postlock-generation` |\n24|| P2-A | attach commits a new receipt after its operation deadline (deadline checked only before the waits) | FIXED — live clock deadline recheck under the lock; the lock wait counts against the deadline; deadline stays distinct from authorization expiry | `TestAttachRefusesDeadlineExpiredDuringAdmission` (operation expired, authorization valid) + `TestAttachRefusesDeadlineOnTheInstantDuringAdmission` via `Lifecycle.Execute`; narrowing `N-attach-postlock-deadline` |\n25|| P2-B | false-to-true input escalation has no effect-level negative witness (receipt commits before the result binding refuses) | FIXED — composed negative test asserting refusal AND receipt absence; landed gate kept, no fork | `TestAttachAuthorizationMembersRefuseWithoutReceipt` (expiry/input/transport) via `Lifecycle.Execute`; narrowing `N-attach-input-escalation` (reviewer A3 shape, cross-package row) |\n26|| P3 | two reported narrowing rows are positive-path wiring mutations (`N-lifecycle-restore/terminate-authkind`) | FIXED — reclassified as supplementary `D-` wiring rows; entry rows converted to genuine no-bind narrowings; new genuinely admitting shared loop mutant with two-entry killers | `TestExecuteEntryRefusesWrongAuthorizationKind` (terminate/restore no-bind), `TestExecuteTerminate/RestoreRefusesAuthorizationExpiredAfterReceipt`; rows `N-entry-authkind-*`, `N-lifecycle-loop-authorization`, `D-lifecycle-*-authkind` |\n27|\n28|## P1+P2-A — one invariant: the effect-boundary fact enumeration\n29|\n30|SPEC §4.C line 1095 (pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`):\n31|\"Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before\n32|each side effect.\" plus \"A deadline cancels waiting, not a\n33|committed effect.\" The attach row allows both\n34|`terminal_backend_stale_generation` and\n35|`terminal_backend_timeout`, so the new refusals are in-row\n36|codes. Every authorization fact the attach path carries:\n37|\n38|| Fact | First observed | Waits before the effect | Revalidated at the effect boundary |\n39||---|---|---|---|\n40|| closure (incarnation-scoped proof) | fast-path check (`ops.go` pre-admission) | server admission + barrier-lock wait | YES — recheck under the lock (rev6, kept) |\n41|| server generation | admission + attestation | barrier-lock wait | YES (new) — live `CurrentGeneration` vs request generation under the lock |\n42|| request deadline | entry check | server admission + barrier-lock wait | YES (new) — live clock under the lock; lock wait counts; distinct from expiry |\n43|| authorization expiry | entry `CheckAttachRequest` | server admission + barrier-lock wait | YES — inside the commit call itself (`AttachStore.Attach` rechecks with the live clock; no wait between its check and the no-replace install) |\n44|| transport binding | entry binding + capability arms | same waits | YES — binding arm inside the commit; capability arm is a pure check over request-immutable `Admitted` (no live fact) |\n45|| input binding | entry `CheckAttachRequest` | same waits | YES — inside the commit, plus the post-commit `CheckAttachResult` |\n46|| transition / operation capability / backend identity | entry checks | same waits | N/A — pure checks over request-immutable members; no live fact to go stale |\n47|| attestation value (fresh vs decoy) | admission | barrier-lock wait | value immutable once returned; its live counterpart is the generation recheck |\n48|\n49|Residual: a rotation landing between the post-lock recheck and\n50|the commit — inside one process or across processes — is not\n51|excluded; the window holds no waits (file I/O only). That is\n52|the B42 in-process scope, extended to the two new rechecks\n53|(B42 text in TRACEABILITY + matrix; code comment cites it).\n54|\n55|The same interval on the other paths: create, quiesce-input,\n56|wait-safe-boundary, and request-stop run through the landed\n57|engine, whose `runEffects` (`internal/terminstance/execute.go`\n58|per-effect deadline, authorization, and generation gates)\n59|rechecks before every effect including the first, after the\n60|receipt bind; terminate-stale and restore run through this\n61|leaf's `runLifecycleEffects` (`ops.go` per-effect deadline,\n62|authorization, and generation gates) with the same shape. No\n63|blocking wait sits between those paths' admission and their\n64|loops (no ServerAdmission, no lock acquisition; the resume\n65|path's status reconcile runs before the loop rechecks), and\n66|status has no side effects so §4.C imposes no recheck on it.\n67|Attach was the only path whose effect lacked a post-wait\n68|revalidation; it now has one. No new bound is stated for the\n69|sibling paths because the per-effect loops already close the\n70|interval by construction.\n71|\n72|Narrowing precision, proven rather than asserted: under the\n73|post-lock-deadline plant the strictly-past test still passes\n74|(only the on-the-instant member is admitted); under the\n75|input-escalation plant the expiry and transport members still\n76|pass; under the loop-authorization plant the positive\n77|terminate/restore tests still pass. The entry-deadline row\n78|needed its own repair: the new post-lock arm is textually\n79|identical to the entry arm, so the row's anchor is now\n80|transition-pinned to the entry site and its killer asserts the\n81|admission never ran — without that assertion the plant would\n82|reroute to the post-lock refusal with the same verdict and\n83|survive.\n84|\n85|## P2-B — the composed authorization witness\n86|\n87|`TestAttachAuthorizationMembersRefuseWithoutReceipt` drives\n88|all three `CheckAttachRequest` members (expiry/input/transport)\n89|through `Execute(attach)` and asserts the landed\n90|`terminal_backend_unauthorized` 