{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c731","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":499,"recorded_at":1780531400000993,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c932-18b2-7002-9e09-e0bd3ea47266"},"task_id":"01a0c932-18b2-7002-9e09-e0bd3ea47266","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c932-18b2-7002-9e09-e0bd3ea47266","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/ops.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"sort\"\n8|\t\"strconv\"\n9|\t\"time\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n16|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n17|)\n18|\n19|// This file executes the three lifecycle operations the landed engine\n20|// scope refuses — attach, terminate-stale, and restore — over the same\n21|// landed gates the engine uses (transition matrix, idempotency shapes,\n22|// authorization, capability conferral, receipt and binding stores)\n23|// plus the tmux backend. The recheck loop, receipt discipline, and\n24|// error-to-observation mapping mirror the engine's second side of each\n25|// rule; the census symmetry lines name both sides.\n26|\n27|// sortedEffects copies effects into bytewise order for the wire.\n28|func sortedEffects(effects []terminalbackend.SideEffect) []terminalbackend.SideEffect {\n29|\tordered := append([]terminalbackend.SideEffect(nil), effects...)\n30|\tsort.Slice(ordered, func(i, j int) bool { return ordered[i] < ordered[j] })\n31|\treturn ordered\n32|}\n33|\n34|// sortedEvidence copies evidence IDs into bytewise order for the wire.\n35|func sortedEvidence(evidence []string) []string {\n36|\tordered := append([]string(nil), evidence...)\n37|\tsort.Strings(ordered)\n38|\treturn ordered\n39|}\n40|\n41|// attachDescriptor derives the bound attach descriptor: socket,\n42|// instance, and client joined by newlines. It is host-local (the\n43|// socket path is usable only on the responding host), deterministic,\n44|// and never persisted: the attach handler returns it without writing\n45|// it anywhere, and a dedicated test scans the stores for its bytes.\n46|// Length is bounded by construction — sun_path socket plus two UUIDs\n47|// stay two orders of magnitude below the 4096 cap — so no length arm\n48|// exists to measure; a test pins the maximum instead.\n49|func attachDescriptor(socket, instance, client string) string {\n50|\treturn socket + \"\\n\" + instance + \"\\n\" + client\n51|}\n52|\n53|// createDescriptor derives the unbound create-interactive descriptor:\n54|// socket and instance only, because create carries no client. Same\n55|// non-persistence and length properties as the bound shape.\n56|func createDescriptor(socket, instance string) string {\n57|\treturn socket + \"\\n\" + instance\n58|}\n59|\n60|// executeAttach runs one attach: closed-shape admission, deadline,\n61|// transition, landed attach authorization, capability conferral plus\n62|// the matching-transport arm, the fast-path quiesce barrier check,\n63|// live server attestation (the P3-A wiring: a fresh decoy admission\n64|// refuses), the authoritative barrier recheck under the ordering\n65|// lock, the durable client receipt, and the caller-executed attach\n66|// vector with its descriptor. The entry returns the vector; it never\n67|// execs an interactive attach.\n68|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeAttach(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n69|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationAttach}\n70|\tbody, err := parseAttachBody(req.Body)\n71|\tif err != nil {\n72|\t\treturn empty, err\n73|\t}\n74|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n75|\t\treturn empty, err\n76|\t}\n77|\tdeadline, err := body.Deadline.Time()\n78|\tif err != nil {\n79|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"attach body deadline\"}\n80|\t}\n81|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n82|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n83|\t}\n84|\tif _, _, err := terminalbackend.CheckTransition(string(terminalbackend.OperationAttach), req.Source, false); err != nil {\n85|\t\treturn empty, err\n86|\t}\n87|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckAttachRequest(body.Authorization, body.Transport, body.InputAuthorized, lc.Now()); err != nil {\n88|\t\treturn empty, err\n89|\t}\n90|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckOperation(string(terminalbackend.OperationAttach), req.Admitted); err != nil {\n91|\t\treturn empty, err\n92|\t}\n93|\tif err := checkAttachTransportCapability(body.Transport, req.Admitted); err != nil {\n94|\t\treturn empty, err\n95|\t}\n96|\tif err := lc.checkAttachQuiesced(body.TerminalInstanceID, body.InputAuthorized); err != nil {\n97|\t\treturn empty, err\n98|\t}\n99|\tif lc.ServerAdmission == nil {\n100|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n101|\t}\n102|\tadmission, err := lc.ServerAdmission()\n103|\tif err != nil {\n104|\t\treturn empty, rowError(terminalbackend.OperationAttach, err)\n105|\t}\n106|\tif err := CheckServerAttested(admission, body.BackendGeneration); err != nil {\n107|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized, Detail: \"attach server attestation\"}\n108|\t}\n109|\t// Ordering contract, attach side: the checks above ran before\n110|\t// the (possibly blocking) server admission and the barrier\n111|\t// lock wait, so every live fact they observed may have gone\n112|\t// stale. The effect boundary below re-observes every live\n113|\t// authorization fact under the lock immediately before the\n114|\t// receipt commit, and the lock holds through the receipt, the\n115|\t// returned vector, and the advisory memory record. The\n116|\t// enumeration, first-observed site to revalidation site:\n117|\t// closure (fast path above, rechecked here); server\n118|\t// generation (admission above, live CurrentGeneration here);\n119|\t// request deadline (entry above, live clock here — the lock\n120|\t// wait counts against the deadline, and the deadline stays\n121|\t// distinct from the authorization expiry); authorization\n122|\t// expiry, transport binding, and input binding (entry\n123|\t// CheckAttachRequest above, live clock rechecked inside the\n124|\t// commit call itself, which holds no wait between its check\n125|\t// and its no-replace install, plus the post-commit result\n126|\t// binding for input). Transition, operation capability, and\n127|\t// backend identity are pure checks over request-immutable\n128|\t// members — no live fact, nothing to revalidate. The\n129|\t// attestation value is immutable once returned; its live\n130|\t// counterpart is the generation rechecked here. Residual: a\n131|\t// rotation landing between this recheck and the commit —\n132|\t// inside one process or across processes — is not excluded;\n133|\t// the window holds no waits (file I/O only). That remainder\n134|\t// is the B42 in-process scope, extended to the generation\n135|\t// and deadline rechecks.\n136|\tlc.barrierMu.Lock()\n137|\tdefer lc.barrierMu.Unlock()\n138|\tif err := lc.checkAttachQuiesced(body.TerminalInstanceID, body.InputAuthorized); err != nil {\n139|\t\treturn empty, err\n140|\t}\n141|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n142|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n143|\t}\n144|\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != body.BackendGeneration {\n145|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n146|\t}\n147|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.SessionID, body.TerminalInstanceID)\n148|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationAttach\n149|\treqBackend.clientID = body.ClientID\n150|\treqBackend.transport = body.Transport\n151|\treqBackend.input = body.InputAuthorized\n152|\treqBackend.authRaw = body.AuthRaw\n153|\tevidenceID, err := reqBackend.PerformEffect(ctx, terminalbackend.EffectAttachClientCreated)\n154|\tif err != nil {\n155|\t\treturn empty, rowError(terminalbackend.OperationAttach, err)\n156|\t}\n157|\targv, err := BuildCommand(DirectiveAttachSession, CommandArgs{\n158|\t\tRuntimeDir:     lc.RuntimeDir,\n159|\t\tSocket:         socket,\n160|\t\tInstanceID:     body.TerminalInstanceID,\n161|\t\tAttachInput:    body.InputAuthorized,\n162|\t\tHasAttachInput: true,\n163|\t})\n164|\tif err != nil {\n165|\t\treturn empty, err\n166|\t}\n167|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckAttachResult(body.InputAuthorized, body.InputAuthorized, body.Authorization); err != nil {\n168|\t\treturn empty, err\n169|\t}\n170|\t// Only an input-authorized attach adopts the active state: a\n171|\t// read-only attach is observation, and recording active for it\n172|\t// would reopen quiesced input (the quiesce barrier reads this\n173|\t// same memory, so observation must leave it untouched).\n174|\tif body.InputAuthorized {\n175|\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(body.TerminalInstanceID, terminalbackend.StateActive)\n176|\t}\n177|\treturn OpOutcome{\n178|\t\tOperation: terminalbackend.OperationAttach,\n179|\t\tAttach: &AttachOutcome{\n180|\t\t\tClientMirrorID:  body.ClientID,\n181|\t\t\tDescriptor:      attachDescriptor(socket, body.TerminalInstanceID, body.ClientID),\n182|\t\t\tInputAuthorized: body.InputAuthorized,\n183|\t\t\tEvidenceIDs:     []string{evidenceID},\n184|\t\t},\n185|\t\tArgv: argv,\n186|\t}, nil\n187|}\n188|\n189|// checkAttachQuiesced enforces the quiesce input barrier at the\n190|// attach entry: tmux offers no session freeze (a locked session does\n191|// not lock subsequently attaching clients), so once a closure\n192|// report proves the input closed in the current incarnation, new\n193|// input-authorized attaches refuse the failed local precondition.\n194|// Read-only attaches stay admitted: quiesce stops input while\n195|// retaining observation. The incarnation-scoped closure proof is the\n196|// sole admission verdict: advisory memory, caller-carried source\n197|// state, and failure reporting are never consulted for their value\n198|// here, so none of them can reopen a closed barrier — a stale\n199|// active record, a failure result echoing its source, and a lost\n200|// state write all refuse exactly like the proof itself. Only a\n201|// fresh create or restore success reopens the input, by rotating\n202|// the incarnation the proof is scoped to. Store health still fails\n203|// closed: an unreadable state record is unknown, never admission,\n204|// so the memory read error propagates even though its value is\n205|// ignored. A proof read failure is likewise an error, never\n206|// admission: unknown is not a verdict.\n207|func (lc *Lifecycle) checkAttachQuiesced(instanceID string, inputAuthorized bool) error {\n208|\tif !inputAuthorized {\n209|\t\treturn nil\n210|\t}\n211|\tif _, _, err := lc.States.Lookup(instanceID); err != nil {\n212|\t\treturn err\n213|\t}\n214|\tproven, err := lc.States.QuiesceBarrierProven(instanceID)\n215|\tif err != nil {\n216|\t\treturn err\n217|\t}\n218|\tif proven {\n219|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"attach quiesced input\"}\n220|\t}\n221|\treturn nil\n222|}\n223|\n224|// checkAttachTransportCapability enforces the matching-transport arm:\n225|// local presentation needs local_attach, mesh presentation needs\n226|// remote_attach. The relay member never reaches here — the landed\n227|// attach authorization refuses it first — so no third arm exists.\n228|func checkAttachTransportCapability(transport string, admitted terminalbackend.Admitted) error {\n229|\tswitch transport {\n230|\tcase string(terminalbackend.TransportLocalOnly):\n231|\t\tif !admitted.Has(\"local_attach\") {\n232|\t\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n233|\t\t}\n234|\tcase string(terminalbackend.TransportTrustedPrivateMesh):\n235|\t\tif !admitted.Has(\"remote_attach\") {\n236|\t\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n237|\t\t}\n238|\tdefault:\n239|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"presentation transport vocabulary\"}\n240|\t}\n241|\treturn nil\n242|}\n243|\n244|// executeTerminate runs one terminate-stale: closed-shape admission,\n245|// idempotency material, capability conferral plus the dual conditional,\n246|// transition, force_stale authorization, generation recheck, landed\n247|// fencing authorization, deadline, receipt discipline with\n248|// status-reconciled resume, and the kill plus close-confirm effects.\n249|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeTerminate(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n250|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale}\n251|\tbody, err := parseTerminateBody(req.Body)\n252|\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\treturn empty, err\n254|\t}\n255|\toperation := terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale\n256|\tmctx := body.Context\n257|\tsource := terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source)\n258|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n259|\t\treturn empty, err\n260|\t}\n261|\tderived, err := terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey(string(operation), mctx.TerminalInstanceID, \"terminate\", body.StaleLeaseID, strconv.FormatUint(body.StaleEpoch, 10))\n262|\tif err != nil {\n263|\t\treturn empty, err\n264|\t}\n265|\tif mctx.IdempotencyKey != derived {\n266|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key material\"}\n267|\t}\n268|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckOperation(string(operation), req.Admitted); err != nil {\n269|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n270|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n271|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n272|\t}\n273|\tif err := checkTerminateCapability(req.Admitted); err != nil {\n274|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n275|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n276|\t}\n277|\ttarget, effects, err := terminalbackend.CheckTransition(string(operation), string(source), false)\n278|\tif err != nil {\n279|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n280|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n281|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n282|\t}\n283|\tif err := terminstance.CheckAuthorization(mctx.Authorization, terminstance.AuthorizationForceStale, lc.CurrentLease(), lc.Now()); err != nil {\n284|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n285|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n286|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n287|\t}\n288|\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != mctx.BackendGeneration {\n289|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n290|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n291|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n292|\t}\n293|\tif err := mapFencingError(fencing.AuthorizeTerminateStale(req.Presented, req.Winner, req.HasWinner, req.ForceRecovery, req.DiagnosticsPreserved)); err != nil {\n294|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n295|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n296|\t}\n297|\tif err := checkTerminateTarget(mctx, body, req.Presented); err != nil {\n298|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n299|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n300|\t}\n301|\tif err := checkTerminateWinner(mctx, req.Winner, lc.CurrentLease()); err != nil {\n302|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n303|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n304|\t}\n305|\tdeadline, err := mctx.Deadline.Time()\n306|\tif err != nil {\n307|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"mutation context deadline\"}\n308|\t}\n309|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n310|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n311|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionReplaySame)\n312|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n313|\t}\n314|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n315|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n316|\treqBackend.deadline = deadline\n317|\treturn lc.executeWithReceipt(ctx, req, socket, operation, mctx, source, target, effects, deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationForceStale, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {\n318|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result, TargetClosed: true}\n319|\t})\n320|}\n321|\n322|// checkTerminateCapability enforces the dual conditional: stale\n323|// termination needs stale_process_termination AND\n324|// provider_process_observation. Each arm refuses alone.\n325|func checkTerminateCapability(admitted terminalbackend.Admitted) error {\n326|\tif !admitted.Has(\"stale_process_termination\") {\n327|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n328|\t}\n329|\tif !admitted.Has(\"provider_process_observation\") {\n330|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n331|\t}\n332|\treturn nil\n333|}\n334|\n335|// mapFencingError maps the landed terminate-stale authorization onto\n336|// the row's allowed set: malformed fencing material is the protocol\n337|// error, every other fencing refusal — no winner, no force, no\n338|// diagnostics, target mismatch, live owner — is the failed local\n339|// precondition. lease_conflict maps to the precondition too: the row\n340|// has no lease_conflict member, and a target fenced by another\n341|// session's winner fails the fenced-target precondition.\n342|func mapFencingError(err error) error {\n343|\tif err == nil {\n344|\t\treturn nil\n345|\t}\n346|\tif errors.Is(err, fencing.ErrInvalidArguments) {\n347|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminate fencing material\"}\n348|\t}\n349|\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"terminate fencing authorization\"}\n350|}\n351|\n352|// checkTerminateTarget binds the presented fencing token to the\n353|// request: session, stale lease, and stale epoch must all agree with\n354|// the context and body. Any disagreement refuses the failed local\n355|// precondition: the retry would authorize a different target than the\n356|// key names.\n357|func checkTerminateTarget(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, body TerminateBody, presented fencing.PresentedToken) error {\n358|\tif presented.SessionID != mctx.SessionID ||\n359|\t\tpresented.LeaseID != body.StaleLeaseID ||\n360|\t\tpresented.Epoch != body.StaleEpoch {\n361|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"terminate target binding\"}\n362|\t}\n363|\treturn nil\n364|}\n365|\n366|// checkTerminateWinner binds the caller-observed winner to the\n367|// re-read current lease: the fencing authorization decides over the\n368|// caller's winner, and only a winner that still wins authorizes. A\n369|// rotated or misobserved winner refuses the failed local\n370|// precondition; the caller re-observes and retries. Absence of a\n371|// winner never reaches here — the fencing gate refuses it first.\n372|func checkTerminateWinner(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, winner sessrepo.LeaseSummary, lease terminstance.LeaseView) error {\n373|\tif winner.SessionID != mctx.SessionID ||\n374|\t\twinner.LeaseID != lease.LeaseID ||\n375|\t\twinner.Epoch != lease.Epoch {\n376|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"terminate winner binding\"}\n377|\t}\n378|\treturn nil\n379|}\n380|\n381|// executeRestore runs one restore: closed-shape admission, idempotency\n382|// material, capability conferral plus the reboot conditional,\n383|// transition, restore authorization, generation recheck, prior-binding\n384|// mismatch, deadline, receipt discipline with status-reconciled\n385|// resume, the persist plus wrapper-restored effects, and the required\n386|// result binding. The wire result is always parked. The backend\n387|// launches no provider: the wrapper owns launch gating through the\n388|// after-restore composition (ExecuteWrapperRestore), and this entry\n389|// only recreates the wrapper process.\n390|//\n391|// The result binding is the create-time document kept alongside the\n392|// bootstrap receipt, re-admitted by termbind on the read — within one\n393|// generation — or its minted successor across a reboot: the termbind\n394|// owner succeeds the prior (the JCS identity rule stays\n395|// termbind-private) and the successor persists under the same pair\n396|// key. The prior-binding mismatch arm proves the carried prior equals\n397|// the recorded digest; the document read proves a valid binding for\n398|// this session, instance, and backend.\n399|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeRestore(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n400|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationRestore}\n401|\tbody, err := parseRestoreBody(req.Body)\n402|\tif err != nil {\n403|\t\treturn empty, err\n404|\t}\n405|\toperation := terminalbackend.OperationRestore\n406|\tmctx := body.Context\n407|\tsource := terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source)\n408|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n409|\t\treturn empty, err\n410|\t}\n411|\tderived, err := terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey(string(operation), mctx.SessionID, body.BootstrapOperationID)\n412|\tif err != nil {\n413|\t\treturn empty, err\n414|\t}\n415|\tif mctx.IdempotencyKey != derived {\n416|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key material\"}\n417|\t}\n418|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckOperation(string(operation), req.Admitted); err != nil {\n419|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n420|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n421|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n422|\t}\n423|\tif !req.Admitted.Has(\"reboot_restoration\") {\n424|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n425|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n426|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n427|\t}\n428|\ttarget, effects, err := terminalbackend.CheckTransition(string(operation), string(source), false)\n429|\tif err != nil {\n430|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n431|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n432|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n433|\t}\n434|\tif err := terminstance.CheckAuthorization(mctx.Authorization, terminstance.AuthorizationRestore, lc.CurrentLease(), lc.Now()); err != nil {\n435|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n436|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n437|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n438|\t}\n439|\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != mctx.BackendGeneration {\n440|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n441|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n442|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n443|\t}\n444|\tif err := lc.checkPriorBinding(body); err != nil {\n445|\t\tvar local *Error\n446|\t\tif errors.As(err, &local) && local.Code == terminalbackend.CodeRestoreMismatch {\n447|\t\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n448|\t\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n449|\t\t}\n450|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeProcessFailed, Detail: \"backend binding read\"}\n451|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n452|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n453|\t}\n454|\tdeadline, err := mctx.Deadline.Time()\n455|\tif err != nil {\n456|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"mutation context deadline\"}\n457|\t}\n458|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n459|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n460|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionReplaySame)\n461|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n462|\t}\n463|\t// The prior binding validates before the receipt binds and the\n464|\t// wrapper recreates: a missing, corrupt, or disagreeing prior\n465|\t// refuses here, never after the irreversible effects.\n466|\tif _, err := lc.readRestorePrior(mctx, body); err != nil {\n467|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n468|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n469|\t}\n470|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n471|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n472|\treqBackend.bootstrapID = body.BootstrapOperationID\n473|\t// The persist effect replays the recorded pair receipt (verified\n474|\t// by the mismatch arm above); the candidate carries the matched\n475|\t// prior digest so the store admits its shape on the replay path.\n476|\treqBackend.bindingID = body.PriorBindingID\n477|\toutcome, err := lc.executeWithReceipt(ctx, req, socket, operation, mctx, source, target, effects, deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationRestore, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {\n478|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result, PriorBindingID: body.PriorBindingID, RestoredParked: true}\n479|\t})\n480|\tif err != nil {\n481|\t\treturn outcome, err\n482|\t}\n483|\tbinding, err := lc.restoreBinding(mctx, body)\n484|\tif err != nil {\n485|\t\treturn outcome, err\n486|\t}\n487|\toutcome.Binding = binding\n488|\treturn outcome, nil\n489|}\n490|\n491|// readRestorePrior reads the create-time binding document kept under\n492|// the (session, bootstrap) pair, re-admitted by the termbind owner,\n493|// and proves it names this restore's session, instance, and backend.\n494|// Generation is not compared here: after a reboot the restore carries\n495|// the new server generation while the prior still names the old one,\n496|// and succession (not agreement) resolves that drift. A missing\n497|// document is the backend store failure — the receipt proved the\n498|// prior, but the payload is gone, so the required result cannot be\n499|// built. A document that fails termbind admission, or that names\n500|// another session, instance, or backend than the mutation context, is\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c733","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":500,"recorded_at":1780531400000995,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c932-18b2-7002-9e09-e0bd3ea47266"},"task_id":"01a0c932-18b2-7002-9e09-e0bd3ea47266","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0c932-18b2-7002-9e09-e0bd3ea47266"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c735","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":501,"recorded_at":1780531400000997,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"call_id":"call_01a0c9321408735daa87c4dfab046926","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/ops.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"sort\"\n8|\t\"strconv\"\n9|\t\"time\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n16|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n17|)\n18|\n19|// This file executes the three lifecycle operations the landed engine\n20|// scope refuses — attach, terminate-stale, and restore — over the same\n21|// landed gates the engine uses (transition matrix, idempotency shapes,\n22|// authorization, capability conferral, receipt and binding stores)\n23|// plus the tmux backend. The recheck loop, receipt discipline, and\n24|// error-to-observation mapping mirror the engine's second side of each\n25|// rule; the census symmetry lines name both sides.\n26|\n27|// sortedEffects copies effects into bytewise order for the wire.\n28|func sortedEffects(effects []terminalbackend.SideEffect) []terminalbackend.SideEffect {\n29|\tordered := append([]terminalbackend.SideEffect(nil), effects...)\n30|\tsort.Slice(ordered, func(i, j int) bool { return ordered[i] < ordered[j] })\n31|\treturn ordered\n32|}\n33|\n34|// sortedEvidence copies evidence IDs into bytewise order for the wire.\n35|func sortedEvidence(evidence []string) []string {\n36|\tordered := append([]string(nil), evidence...)\n37|\tsort.Strings(ordered)\n38|\treturn ordered\n39|}\n40|\n41|// attachDescriptor derives the bound attach descriptor: socket,\n42|// instance, and client joined by newlines. It is host-local (the\n43|// socket path is usable only on the responding host), deterministic,\n44|// and never persisted: the attach handler returns it without writing\n45|// it anywhere, and a dedicated test scans the stores for its bytes.\n46|// Length is bounded by construction — sun_path socket plus two UUIDs\n47|// stay two orders of magnitude below the 4096 cap — so no length arm\n48|// exists to measure; a test pins the maximum instead.\n49|func attachDescriptor(socket, instance, client string) string {\n50|\treturn socket + \"\\n\" + instance + \"\\n\" + client\n51|}\n52|\n53|// createDescriptor derives the unbound create-interactive descriptor:\n54|// socket and instance only, because create carries no client. Same\n55|// non-persistence and length properties as the bound shape.\n56|func createDescriptor(socket, instance string) string {\n57|\treturn socket + \"\\n\" + instance\n58|}\n59|\n60|// executeAttach runs one attach: closed-shape admission, deadline,\n61|// transition, landed attach authorization, capability conferral plus\n62|// the matching-transport arm, the fast-path quiesce barrier check,\n63|// live server attestation (the P3-A wiring: a fresh decoy admission\n64|// refuses), the authoritative barrier recheck under the ordering\n65|// lock, the durable client receipt, and the caller-executed attach\n66|// vector with its descriptor. The entry returns the vector; it never\n67|// execs an interactive attach.\n68|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeAttach(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n69|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationAttach}\n70|\tbody, err := parseAttachBody(req.Body)\n71|\tif err != nil {\n72|\t\treturn empty, err\n73|\t}\n74|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n75|\t\treturn empty, err\n76|\t}\n77|\tdeadline, err := body.Deadline.Time()\n78|\tif err != nil {\n79|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"attach body deadline\"}\n80|\t}\n81|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n82|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n83|\t}\n84|\tif _, _, err := terminalbackend.CheckTransition(string(terminalbackend.OperationAttach), req.Source, false); err != nil {\n85|\t\treturn empty, err\n86|\t}\n87|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckAttachRequest(body.Authorization, body.Transport, body.InputAuthorized, lc.Now()); err != nil {\n88|\t\treturn empty, err\n89|\t}\n90|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckOperation(string(terminalbackend.OperationAttach), req.Admitted); err != nil {\n91|\t\treturn empty, err\n92|\t}\n93|\tif err := checkAttachTransportCapability(body.Transport, req.Admitted); err != nil {\n94|\t\treturn empty, err\n95|\t}\n96|\tif err := lc.checkAttachQuiesced(body.TerminalInstanceID, body.InputAuthorized); err != nil {\n97|\t\treturn empty, err\n98|\t}\n99|\tif lc.ServerAdmission == nil {\n100|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n101|\t}\n102|\tadmission, err := lc.ServerAdmission()\n103|\tif err != nil {\n104|\t\treturn empty, rowError(terminalbackend.OperationAttach, err)\n105|\t}\n106|\tif err := CheckServerAttested(admission, body.BackendGeneration); err != nil {\n107|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized, Detail: \"attach server attestation\"}\n108|\t}\n109|\t// Ordering contract, attach side: the checks above ran before\n110|\t// the (possibly blocking) server admission and the barrier\n111|\t// lock wait, so every live fact they observed may have gone\n112|\t// stale. The effect boundary below re-observes every live\n113|\t// authorization fact under the lock immediately before the\n114|\t// receipt commit, and the lock holds through the receipt, the\n115|\t// returned vector, and the advisory memory record. The\n116|\t// enumeration, first-observed site to revalidation site:\n117|\t// closure (fast path above, rechecked here); server\n118|\t// generation (admission above, live CurrentGeneration here);\n119|\t// request deadline (entry above, live clock here — the lock\n120|\t// wait counts against the deadline, and the deadline stays\n121|\t// distinct from the authorization expiry); authorization\n122|\t// expiry, transport binding, and input binding (entry\n123|\t// CheckAttachRequest above, live clock rechecked inside the\n124|\t// commit call itself, which holds no wait between its check\n125|\t// and its no-replace install, plus the post-commit result\n126|\t// binding for input). Transition, operation capability, and\n127|\t// backend identity are pure checks over request-immutable\n128|\t// members — no live fact, nothing to revalidate. The\n129|\t// attestation value is immutable once returned; its live\n130|\t// counterpart is the generation rechecked here. Residual: a\n131|\t// rotation landing between this recheck and the commit —\n132|\t// inside one process or across processes — is not excluded;\n133|\t// the window holds no waits (file I/O only). That remainder\n134|\t// is the B42 in-process scope, extended to the generation\n135|\t// and deadline rechecks.\n136|\tlc.barrierMu.Lock()\n137|\tdefer lc.barrierMu.Unlock()\n138|\tif err := lc.checkAttachQuiesced(body.TerminalInstanceID, body.InputAuthorized); err != nil {\n139|\t\treturn empty, err\n140|\t}\n141|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n142|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n143|\t}\n144|\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != body.BackendGeneration {\n145|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n146|\t}\n147|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.SessionID, body.TerminalInstanceID)\n148|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationAttach\n149|\treqBackend.clientID = body.ClientID\n150|\treqBackend.transport = body.Transport\n151|\treqBackend.input = body.InputAuthorized\n152|\treqBackend.authRaw = body.AuthRaw\n153|\tevidenceID, err := reqBackend.PerformEffect(ctx, terminalbackend.EffectAttachClientCreated)\n154|\tif err != nil {\n155|\t\treturn empty, rowError(terminalbackend.OperationAttach, err)\n156|\t}\n157|\targv, err := BuildCommand(DirectiveAttachSession, CommandArgs{\n158|\t\tRuntimeDir:     lc.RuntimeDir,\n159|\t\tSocket:         socket,\n160|\t\tInstanceID:     body.TerminalInstanceID,\n161|\t\tAttachInput:    body.InputAuthorized,\n162|\t\tHasAttachInput: true,\n163|\t})\n164|\tif err != nil {\n165|\t\treturn empty, err\n166|\t}\n167|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckAttachResult(body.InputAuthorized, body.InputAuthorized, body.Authorization); err != nil {\n168|\t\treturn empty, err\n169|\t}\n170|\t// Only an input-authorized attach adopts the active state: a\n171|\t// read-only attach is observation, and recording active for it\n172|\t// would reopen quiesced input (the quiesce barrier reads this\n173|\t// same memory, so observation must leave it untouched).\n174|\tif body.InputAuthorized {\n175|\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(body.TerminalInstanceID, terminalbackend.StateActive)\n176|\t}\n177|\treturn OpOutcome{\n178|\t\tOperation: terminalbackend.OperationAttach,\n179|\t\tAttach: &AttachOutcome{\n180|\t\t\tClientMirrorID:  body.ClientID,\n181|\t\t\tDescriptor:      attachDescriptor(socket, body.TerminalInstanceID, body.ClientID),\n182|\t\t\tInputAuthorized: body.InputAuthorized,\n183|\t\t\tEvidenceIDs:     []string{evidenceID},\n184|\t\t},\n185|\t\tArgv: argv,\n186|\t}, nil\n187|}\n188|\n189|// checkAttachQuiesced enforces the quiesce input barrier at the\n190|// attach entry: tmux offers no session freeze (a locked session does\n191|// not lock subsequently attaching clients), so once a closure\n192|// report proves the input closed in the current incarnation, new\n193|// input-authorized attaches refuse the failed local precondition.\n194|// Read-only attaches stay admitted: quiesce stops input while\n195|// retaining observation. The incarnation-scoped closure proof is the\n196|// sole admission verdict: advisory memory, caller-carried source\n197|// state, and failure reporting are never consulted for their value\n198|// here, so none of them can reopen a closed barrier — a stale\n199|// active record, a failure result echoing its source, and a lost\n200|// state write all refuse exactly like the proof itself. Only a\n201|// fresh create or restore success reopens the input, by rotating\n202|// the incarnation the proof is scoped to. Store health still fails\n203|// closed: an unreadable state record is unknown, never admission,\n204|// so the memory read error propagates even though its value is\n205|// ignored. A proof read failure is likewise an error, never\n206|// admission: unknown is not a verdict.\n207|func (lc *Lifecycle) checkAttachQuiesced(instanceID string, inputAuthorized bool) error {\n208|\tif !inputAuthorized {\n209|\t\treturn nil\n210|\t}\n211|\tif _, _, err := lc.States.Lookup(instanceID); err != nil {\n212|\t\treturn err\n213|\t}\n214|\tproven, err := lc.States.QuiesceBarrierProven(instanceID)\n215|\tif err != nil {\n216|\t\treturn err\n217|\t}\n218|\tif proven {\n219|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"attach quiesced input\"}\n220|\t}\n221|\treturn nil\n222|}\n223|\n224|// checkAttachTransportCapability enforces the matching-transport arm:\n225|// local presentation needs local_attach, mesh presentation needs\n226|// remote_attach. The relay member never reaches here — the landed\n227|// attach authorization refuses it first — so no third arm exists.\n228|func checkAttachTransportCapability(transport string, admitted terminalbackend.Admitted) error {\n229|\tswitch transport {\n230|\tcase string(terminalbackend.TransportLocalOnly):\n231|\t\tif !admitted.Has(\"local_attach\") {\n232|\t\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n233|\t\t}\n234|\tcase string(terminalbackend.TransportTrustedPrivateMesh):\n235|\t\tif !admitted.Has(\"remote_attach\") {\n236|\t\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n237|\t\t}\n238|\tdefault:\n239|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"presentation transport vocabulary\"}\n240|\t}\n241|\treturn nil\n242|}\n243|\n244|// executeTerminate runs one terminate-stale: closed-shape admission,\n245|// idempotency material, capability conferral plus the dual conditional,\n246|// transition, force_stale authorization, generation recheck, landed\n247|// fencing authorization, deadline, receipt discipline with\n248|// status-reconciled resume, and the kill plus close-confirm effects.\n249|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeTerminate(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n250|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale}\n251|\tbody, err := parseTerminateBody(req.Body)\n252|\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\treturn empty, err\n254|\t}\n255|\toperation := terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale\n256|\tmctx := body.Context\n257|\tsource := terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source)\n258|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n259|\t\treturn empty, err\n260|\t}\n261|\tderived, err := terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey(string(operation), mctx.TerminalInstanceID, \"terminate\", body.StaleLeaseID, strconv.FormatUint(body.StaleEpoch, 10))\n262|\tif err != nil {\n263|\t\treturn empty, err\n264|\t}\n265|\tif mctx.IdempotencyKey != derived {\n266|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key material\"}\n267|\t}\n268|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckOperation(string(operation), req.Admitted); err != nil {\n269|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n270|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n271|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n272|\t}\n273|\tif err := checkTerminateCapability(req.Admitted); err != nil {\n274|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n275|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n276|\t}\n277|\ttarget, effects, err := terminalbackend.CheckTransition(string(operation), string(source), false)\n278|\tif err != nil {\n279|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n280|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n281|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n282|\t}\n283|\tif err := terminstance.CheckAuthorization(mctx.Authorization, terminstance.AuthorizationForceStale, lc.CurrentLease(), lc.Now()); err != nil {\n284|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n285|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n286|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n287|\t}\n288|\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != mctx.BackendGeneration {\n289|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n290|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n291|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n292|\t}\n293|\tif err := mapFencingError(fencing.AuthorizeTerminateStale(req.Presented, req.Winner, req.HasWinner, req.ForceRecovery, req.DiagnosticsPreserved)); err != nil {\n294|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n295|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n296|\t}\n297|\tif err := checkTerminateTarget(mctx, body, req.Presented); err != nil {\n298|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n299|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n300|\t}\n301|\tif err := checkTerminateWinner(mctx, req.Winner, lc.CurrentLease()); err != nil {\n302|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n303|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n304|\t}\n305|\tdeadline, err := mctx.Deadline.Time()\n306|\tif err != nil {\n307|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"mutation context deadline\"}\n308|\t}\n309|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n310|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n311|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionReplaySame)\n312|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n313|\t}\n314|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n315|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n316|\treqBackend.deadline = deadline\n317|\treturn lc.executeWithReceipt(ctx, req, socket, operation, mctx, source, target, effects, deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationForceStale, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {\n318|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result, TargetClosed: true}\n319|\t})\n320|}\n321|\n322|// checkTerminateCapability enforces the dual conditional: stale\n323|// termination needs stale_process_termination AND\n324|// provider_process_observation. Each arm refuses alone.\n325|func checkTerminateCapability(admitted terminalbackend.Admitted) error {\n326|\tif !admitted.Has(\"stale_process_termination\") {\n327|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n328|\t}\n329|\tif !admitted.Has(\"provider_process_observation\") {\n330|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n331|\t}\n332|\treturn nil\n333|}\n334|\n335|// mapFencingError maps the landed terminate-stale authorization onto\n336|// the row's allowed set: malformed fencing material is the protocol\n337|// error, every other fencing refusal — no winner, no force, no\n338|// diagnostics, target mismatch, live owner — is the failed local\n339|// precondition. lease_conflict maps to the precondition too: the row\n340|// has no lease_conflict member, and a target fenced by another\n341|// session's winner fails the fenced-target precondition.\n342|func mapFencingError(err error) error {\n343|\tif err == nil {\n344|\t\treturn nil\n345|\t}\n346|\tif errors.Is(err, fencing.ErrInvalidArguments) {\n347|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminate fencing material\"}\n348|\t}\n349|\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"terminate fencing authorization\"}\n350|}\n351|\n352|// checkTerminateTarget binds the presented fencing token to the\n353|// request: session, stale lease, and stale epoch must all agree with\n354|// the context and body. Any disagreement refuses the failed local\n355|// precondition: the retry would authorize a different target than the\n356|// key names.\n357|func checkTerminateTarget(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, body TerminateBody, presented fencing.PresentedToken) error {\n358|\tif presented.SessionID != mctx.SessionID ||\n359|\t\tpresented.LeaseID != body.StaleLeaseID ||\n360|\t\tpresented.Epoch != body.StaleEpoch {\n361|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"terminate target binding\"}\n362|\t}\n363|\treturn nil\n364|}\n365|\n366|// checkTerminateWinner binds the caller-observed winner to the\n367|// re-read current lease: the fencing authorization decides over the\n368|// caller's winner, and only a winner that still wins authorizes. A\n369|// rotated or misobserved winner refuses the failed local\n370|// precondition; the caller re-observes and retries. Absence of a\n371|// winner never reaches here — the fencing gate refuses it first.\n372|func checkTerminateWinner(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, winner sessrepo.LeaseSummary, lease terminstance.LeaseView) error {\n373|\tif winner.SessionID != mctx.SessionID ||\n374|\t\twinner.LeaseID != lease.LeaseID ||\n375|\t\twinner.Epoch != lease.Epoch {\n376|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"terminate winner binding\"}\n377|\t}\n378|\treturn nil\n379|}\n380|\n381|// executeRestore runs one restore: closed-shape admission, idempotency\n382|// material, capability conferral plus the reboot conditional,\n383|// transition, restore authorization, generation recheck, prior-binding\n384|// mismatch, deadline, receipt discipline with status-reconciled\n385|// resume, the persist plus wrapper-restored effects, and the required\n386|// result binding. The wire result is always parked. The backend\n387|// launches no provider: the wrapper owns launch gating through the\n388|// after-restore composition (ExecuteWrapperRestore), and this entry\n389|// only recreates the wrapper process.\n390|//\n391|// The result binding is the create-time document kept alongside the\n392|// bootstrap receipt, re-admitted by termbind on the read — within one\n393|// generation — or its minted successor across a reboot: the termbind\n394|// owner succeeds the prior (the JCS identity rule stays\n395|// termbind-private) and the successor persists under the same pair\n396|// key. The prior-binding mismatch arm proves the carried prior equals\n397|// the recorded digest; the document read proves a valid binding for\n398|// this session, instance, and backend.\n399|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeRestore(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n400|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationRestore}\n401|\tbody, err := parseRestoreBody(req.Body)\n402|\tif err != nil {\n403|\t\treturn empty, err\n404|\t}\n405|\toperation := terminalbackend.OperationRestore\n406|\tmctx := body.Context\n407|\tsource := terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source)\n408|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n409|\t\treturn empty, err\n410|\t}\n411|\tderived, err := terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey(string(operation), mctx.SessionID, body.BootstrapOperationID)\n412|\tif err != nil {\n413|\t\treturn empty, err\n414|\t}\n415|\tif mctx.IdempotencyKey != derived {\n416|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"idempotency key material\"}\n417|\t}\n418|\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckOperation(string(operation), req.Admitted); err != nil {\n419|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n420|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n421|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n422|\t}\n423|\tif !req.Admitted.Has(\"reboot_restoration\") {\n424|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven, Detail: \"operation capability conditional\"}\n425|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n426|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n427|\t}\n428|\ttarget, effects, err := terminalbackend.CheckTransition(string(operation), string(source), false)\n429|\tif err != nil {\n430|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n431|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n432|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n433|\t}\n434|\tif err := terminstance.CheckAuthorization(mctx.Authorization, terminstance.AuthorizationRestore, lc.CurrentLease(), lc.Now()); err != nil {\n435|\t\tfailure := rowError(operation, err)\n436|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n437|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n438|\t}\n439|\tif lc.CurrentGeneration() != mctx.BackendGeneration {\n440|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration, Detail: \"backend_generation stale\"}\n441|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n442|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n443|\t}\n444|\tif err := lc.checkPriorBinding(body); err != nil {\n445|\t\tvar local *Error\n446|\t\tif errors.As(err, &local) && local.Code == terminalbackend.CodeRestoreMismatch {\n447|\t\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n448|\t\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n449|\t\t}\n450|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeProcessFailed, Detail: \"backend binding read\"}\n451|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(failure), false))\n452|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n453|\t}\n454|\tdeadline, err := mctx.Deadline.Time()\n455|\tif err != nil {\n456|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"mutation context deadline\"}\n457|\t}\n458|\tif !lc.Now().Before(deadline) {\n459|\t\tfailure := &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeTimeout, Detail: \"operation deadline\"}\n460|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionReplaySame)\n461|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, failure\n462|\t}\n463|\t// The prior binding validates before the receipt binds and the\n464|\t// wrapper recreates: a missing, corrupt, or disagreeing prior\n465|\t// refuses here, never after the irreversible effects.\n466|\tif _, err := lc.readRestorePrior(mctx, body); err != nil {\n467|\t\tresult := mutationResult(mctx, source, source, nil, nil, terminstance.DispositionFor(backendErrorCode(err), false))\n468|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result}, err\n469|\t}\n470|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n471|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n472|\treqBackend.bootstrapID = body.BootstrapOperationID\n473|\t// The persist effect replays the recorded pair receipt (verified\n474|\t// by the mismatch arm above); the candidate carries the matched\n475|\t// prior digest so the store admits its shape on the replay path.\n476|\treqBackend.bindingID = body.PriorBindingID\n477|\toutcome, err := lc.executeWithReceipt(ctx, req, socket, operation, mctx, source, target, effects, deadline, terminstance.AuthorizationRestore, reqBackend, func(result terminstance.Result) OpOutcome {\n478|\t\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: operation, Mutation: &result, PriorBindingID: body.PriorBindingID, RestoredParked: true}\n479|\t})\n480|\tif err != nil {\n481|\t\treturn outcome, err\n482|\t}\n483|\tbinding, err := lc.restoreBinding(mctx, body)\n484|\tif err != nil {\n485|\t\treturn outcome, err\n486|\t}\n487|\toutcome.Binding = binding\n488|\treturn outcome, nil\n489|}\n490|\n491|// readRestorePrior reads the create-time binding document kept under\n492|// the (session, bootstrap) pair, re-admitted by the termbind owner,\n493|// and proves it names this restore's session, instance, and backend.\n494|// Generation is not compared here: after a reboot the restore carries\n495|// the new server generation while the prior still names the old one,\n496|// and succession (not agreement) resolves that drift. A missing\n497|// document is the backend store failure — the receipt proved the\n498|// prior, but the payload is gone, so the required result cannot be\n499|// built. A document that fails termbind admission, or that names\n500|// another session, instance, or backend than the mutation context, is\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
