{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":545,"recorded_at":1780531400001085,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c932-3099-7143-9cf3-dd25bd3070ae"},"task_id":"01a0c932-3099-7143-9cf3-dd25bd3070ae","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c932-3099-7143-9cf3-dd25bd3070ae","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"sync\"\n6|\t\"time\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n15|)\n16|\n17|// Lifecycle executes the eight tmux lifecycle operations — create,\n18|// attach, status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n19|// terminate-stale, restore — over the structured commands. Five\n20|// operations (create, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n21|// status) delegate to the landed terminstance engine with the tmux\n22|// backend; attach, terminate-stale, and restore — which the engine\n23|// scope gate refuses — execute here over the same landed gates\n24|// (transition matrix, idempotency shapes, authorization, capability\n25|// conferral, receipt and binding stores) plus the tmux backend.\n26|//\n27|// A Lifecycle is constructed whole: every store and function value is\n28|// required (except Sleep/PollInterval, which default, and\n29|// ServerAdmission, which only attach needs). The Execute entry refuses\n30|// before any work when a dependency is missing.\n31|type Lifecycle struct {\n32|\t// RuntimeDir is the tmux runtime directory (<root>/tmux) the\n33|\t// socket derives from.\n34|\tRuntimeDir string\n35|\t// Root is the Runtime IPC root the socket custody verifies.\n36|\tRoot string\n37|\t// Platform selects the sun_path limit.\n38|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n39|\t// Runner executes the tmux commands.\n40|\tRunner Runner\n41|\t// Receipts is the durable idempotency receipt table.\n42|\tReceipts *terminstance.ReceiptStore\n43|\t// Bindings is the durable bootstrap binding store.\n44|\tBindings *axpane.Store\n45|\t// Attach is the durable attach-client receipt store.\n46|\tAttach *termbind.AttachStore\n47|\t// States is the durable AX-side state memory.\n48|\tStates *InstanceStates\n49|\t// CurrentLease and CurrentGeneration re-read the winning lease\n50|\t// and the validated binding generation at every check point.\n51|\tCurrentLease      func() terminstance.LeaseView\n52|\tCurrentGeneration func() string\n53|\t// Now is the clock.\n54|\tNow func() time.Time\n55|\t// Sleep waits between close-confirm polls. Nil means time.Sleep.\n56|\tSleep func(time.Duration)\n57|\t// PollInterval separates close-confirm polls. Non-positive means\n58|\t// 50 milliseconds.\n59|\tPollInterval time.Duration\n60|\t// ServerAdmission reports the live server attestation the attach\n61|\t// handler binds to the request generation (the P3-A wiring: a\n62|\t// fresh decoy admission refuses here). Nil refuses attach only.\n63|\tServerAdmission func() (RealmAdmission, error)\n64|\t// LocalHostID is the AX host identity the after-restore\n65|\t// composition compares the winning lease holder against. Empty\n66|\t// cannot prove a local win, so the composition parks or offers\n67|\t// remote attach only, never resumes.\n68|\tLocalHostID string\n69|\t// LeaseRefresh attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh\n70|\t// (after-restore step 2) under a timeout context. Nil skips the\n71|\t// attempt; a failed attempt also falls back to local knowledge.\n72|\t// Only a successful refresh verifies: the fallback decides\n73|\t// unverified, so it parks instead of resuming.\n74|\tLeaseRefresh func(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (RefreshWinner, error)\n75|\t// MeshRefreshTimeout bounds one refresh attempt. Non-positive\n76|\t// means DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout. The bound is enforced, not\n77|\t// advisory: the entry returns at the deadline even against an\n78|\t// adapter that ignores cancellation, and a late answer never\n79|\t// verifies.\n80|\tMeshRefreshTimeout time.Duration\n81|\t// Hooks observes receipts and effects. Nil disables observation.\n82|\tHooks *terminstance.EngineHooks\n83|\t// RefreshHooks arms the race boundary of the refresh select.\n84|\t// Nil in production.\n85|\tRefreshHooks *RefreshHooks\n86|\t// barrierMu serializes the input-closure ordering contract: the\n87|\t// quiesce report commit, the boundary report commit, and the\n88|\t// attach writable-receipt commit (barrier recheck, client\n89|\t// receipt, returned vector, advisory memory) are mutually\n90|\t// exclusive, so whichever lands first wins and no writable\n91|\t// receipt commits after a durable closure report. The initial\n92|\t// attach fast-path check and the server admission run outside\n93|\t// the lock (admission may block); only the recheck-to-vector\n94|\t// section holds it. The quiesce engine closure runs inside the\n95|\t// lock (its tmux effects return immediately); the boundary wait\n96|\t// runs outside (it blocks on the wrapper signal) and only its\n97|\t// report commit takes the lock. Non-reentrant: hooks firing\n98|\t// inside a locked section must not call Execute. The contract\n99|\t// is in-process: concurrent ax processes racing attach against\n100|\t// quiesce serialize only through the report files, not through\n101|\t// this mutex (bound B42). The vector handoff the contract\n102|\t// covers ends at vector construction: a caller that execs a\n103|\t// pre-quiescence vector after quiescence commits holds a\n104|\t// pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\n105|\tbarrierMu sync.Mutex\n106|}\n107|\n108|// RefreshHooks arms the race boundary of the mesh lease refresh:\n109|// BeforeSelect runs after the adapter launches and before the entry\n110|// selects over the answer and the deadline. A nil hook is a no-op.\n111|// Tests stall past the bound to force the both-ready race\n112|// deterministically: without the stall the deadline arm always wins\n113|// and the answer-path expiry check never triggers.\n114|type RefreshHooks struct {\n115|\tBeforeSelect func()\n116|}\n117|\n118|// DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout bounds the after-restore mesh lease\n119|// refresh when the Lifecycle leaves it unset: five seconds, after\n120|// which the branch proceeds on local knowledge instead of blocking\n121|// forever.\n122|const DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout = 5 * time.Second\n123|\n124|// RefreshWinner is one mesh lease-refresh answer: the winning lease\n125|// tuple and its holder host.\n126|type RefreshWinner struct {\n127|\tLeaseID      string\n128|\tEpoch        uint64\n129|\tHolderHostID string\n130|}\n131|\n132|// OpRequest is one lifecycle operation request: the operation name,\n133|// its closed body, the presented source state, the admitted\n134|// capabilities, and the fencing material (for terminate-stale only).\n135|type OpRequest struct {\n136|\tOperation            string\n137|\tBody                 []byte\n138|\tSource               string\n139|\tAdmitted             terminalbackend.Admitted\n140|\tPresented            fencing.PresentedToken\n141|\tWinner               sessrepo.LeaseSummary\n142|\tHasWinner            bool\n143|\tForceRecovery        bool\n144|\tDiagnosticsPreserved bool\n145|}\n146|\n147|// AttachOutcome is the attach success payload: the client mirror, the\n148|// host-local descriptor, the authorized input boolean, and the\n149|// evidence. The result input boolean always equals the request and the\n150|// authorization; the landed CheckAttachResult proves it on every call.\n151|type AttachOutcome struct {\n152|\tClientMirrorID  string\n153|\tDescriptor      string\n154|\tInputAuthorized bool\n155|\tEvidenceIDs     []string\n156|}\n157|\n158|// OpOutcome is one executed operation: exactly one of Mutation,\n159|// Status, or Attach is set, plus the per-operation success members.\n160|// Mutation is set on every executed mutating path — success and\n161|// coded failure alike, mirroring the engine — and nil only when the\n162|// request was malformed before any result existed.\n163|type OpOutcome struct {\n164|\tOperation              terminalbackend.Operation\n165|\tMutation               *terminstance.Result\n166|\tStatus                 *terminstance.StatusReport\n167|\tAttach                 *AttachOutcome\n168|\tArgv                   []string\n169|\tBinding                *termbind.Binding\n170|\tDescriptor             *string\n171|\tPriorBindingID         string\n172|\tRestoredParked         bool\n173|\tTargetClosed           bool\n174|\tProcessClosed          bool\n175|\tStoreClosed            bool\n176|\tQuiescenceGeneration   string\n177|\tInputClosedAt          string\n178|\tSafeBoundaryEvidenceID string\n179|\tBoundaryObservedAt     string\n180|}\n181|\n182|// Execute runs one lifecycle operation to its outcome. Refusals\n183|// precede side effects: malformed operations, unknown backends, and\n184|// unsafe sockets refuse before any store or tmux interaction. The\n185|// socket custody (before-connect rejection) and length refusal run on\n186|// every operation, because every operation connects.\n187|func (lc *Lifecycle) Execute(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest) (OpOutcome, error) {\n188|\tempty := OpOutcome{}\n189|\tif lc == nil || lc.Runner == nil || lc.Receipts == nil || lc.Bindings == nil ||\n190|\t\tlc.Attach == nil || lc.States == nil ||\n191|\t\tlc.CurrentLease == nil || lc.CurrentGeneration == nil || lc.Now == nil {\n192|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n193|\t}\n194|\toperation, err := terminalbackend.ParseOperation(req.Operation)\n195|\tif err != nil {\n196|\t\treturn empty, err\n197|\t}\n198|\tif _, err := DirectivesFor(operation); err != nil {\n199|\t\treturn empty, err\n200|\t}\n201|\tsocket := SocketPath(lc.RuntimeDir)\n202|\tif err := CheckSocketLength(socket, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n203|\t\treturn empty, err\n204|\t}\n205|\tif err := CheckSocketCustody(socket, lc.Root, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n206|\t\treturn empty, err\n207|\t}\n208|\tswitch operation {\n209|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationCreate:\n210|\t\treturn lc.executeCreate(ctx, req, socket)\n211|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationAttach:\n212|\t\treturn lc.executeAttach(ctx, req, socket)\n213|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationStatus:\n214|\t\treturn lc.executeStatus(ctx, req, socket)\n215|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\n216|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n217|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n218|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n219|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n220|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n221|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale:\n222|\t\treturn lc.executeTerminate(ctx, req, socket)\n223|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRestore:\n224|\t\treturn lc.executeRestore(ctx, req, socket)\n225|\tdefault:\n226|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle operation\"}\n227|\t}\n228|}\n229|\n230|// engineFor builds the per-call landed engine over a request-scoped\n231|// tmux backend. The engine is a plain struct: constructing one per\n232|// call keeps request identity out of shared state.\n233|func (lc *Lifecycle) engineFor(reqBackend *backend) *terminstance.Engine {\n234|\treturn &terminstance.Engine{\n235|\t\tStore:             lc.Receipts,\n236|\t\tBackend:           reqBackend,\n237|\t\tCurrentLease:      lc.CurrentLease,\n238|\t\tCurrentGeneration: lc.CurrentGeneration,\n239|\t\tNow:               lc.Now,\n240|\t\tHooks:             lc.Hooks,\n241|\t}\n242|}\n243|\n244|// requestBackend builds the request-scoped tmux backend over the\n245|// lifecycle stores and the admitted set.\n246|func (lc *Lifecycle) requestBackend(req OpRequest, socket, session, instance string) *backend {\n247|\tsleep := lc.Sleep\n248|\tif sleep == nil {\n249|\t\tsleep = time.Sleep\n250|\t}\n251|\tpoll := lc.PollInterval\n252|\tif poll <= 0 {\n253|\t\tpoll = 50 * time.Millisecond\n254|\t}\n255|\treturn &backend{\n256|\t\trunner:     lc.Runner,\n257|\t\truntimeDir: lc.RuntimeDir,\n258|\t\tsocket:     socket,\n259|\t\tsessionID:  session,\n260|\t\tinstanceID: instance,\n261|\t\tnow:        lc.Now,\n262|\t\tsleep:      sleep,\n263|\t\tpoll:       poll,\n264|\t\tadmitted:   req.Admitted,\n265|\t\tbindings:   lc.Bindings,\n266|\t\tattach:     lc.Attach,\n267|\t\tstates:     lc.States,\n268|\t\tkillExit:   -1,\n269|\t}\n270|}\n271|\n272|// recordAfter records the adopted after-state in the AX-side memory on\n273|// success paths. The memory is advisory everywhere: status\n274|// reconciles the live probe against it, but attach admission never\n275|// consults it — only the incarnation-scoped closure proof decides\n276|// admission, so a stale or lost memory record can neither reopen a\n277|// closed barrier nor close an open one. On the barrier successes\n278|// (quiesce-input and wait-safe-boundary) the caller still checks the\n279|// returned error and fails closed, keeping the status memory\n280|// faithful to the closure the operation just proved.\n281|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordAfter(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) error {\n282|\tif lc.States == nil {\n283|\t\treturn nil\n284|\t}\n285|\treturn lc.States.Record(instance, after)\n286|}\n287|\n288|// recordFailure records the after-state of a failed operation. A\n289|// failure with committed effects and an uncertain tail (After\n290|// unavailable) overwrites with the honest unknown: the prior record\n291|// no longer describes the instance. A pure refusal proves nothing —\n292|// its After echoes the caller-carried source — so it installs that\n293|// echo only when the memory holds no record at all (letting the\n294|// uncertain-resume path reconcile a first-operation failure) and\n295|// never overwrites an authoritative record with stale caller state.\n296|// Failure reporting can never reopen a closed barrier: attach\n297|// admission never consults this memory, and a refusal either\n298|// preserves the prior record, installs a first echo, or records the\n299|// non-admitting unknown.\n300|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordFailure(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) {\n301|\tif lc.States == nil {\n302|\t\treturn\n303|\t}\n304|\tif after == terminalbackend.StateUnavailable {\n305|\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(instance, after)\n306|\t\treturn\n307|\t}\n308|\t_, found, err := lc.States.Lookup(instance)\n309|\tif err != nil || found {\n310|\t\treturn\n311|\t}\n312|\t_ = lc.recordAfter(instance, after)\n313|}\n314|\n315|// mutationResult assembles a lifecycle result with the engine's\n316|// buildResult contract: repeated request identities, before/after\n317|// states, bytewise-sorted effects and evidence, and one disposition.\n318|func mutationResult(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, before, after terminalbackend.InstanceState, effects []terminalbackend.SideEffect, evidence []string, disposition terminstance.RetryDisposition) terminstance.Result {\n319|\treturn terminstance.Result{\n320|\t\tOperationID:           mctx.OperationID,\n321|\t\tSessionID:             mctx.SessionID,\n322|\t\tTerminalInstanceID:    mctx.TerminalInstanceID,\n323|\t\tTerminalBackendID:     mctx.TerminalBackendID,\n324|\t\tImplementationVersion: mctx.ImplementationVersion,\n325|\t\tProtocolVersion:       mctx.ProtocolVersion,\n326|\t\tBackendGeneration:     mctx.BackendGeneration,\n327|\t\tBefore:                before,\n328|\t\tAfter:                 after,\n329|\t\tEffects:               sortedEffects(effects),\n330|\t\tEvidenceIDs:           sortedEvidence(evidence),\n331|\t\tDisposition:           disposition,\n332|\t}\n333|}\n334|\n335|// checkLifecycleBackend admits exactly the tmux backend identity: this\n336|// lifecycle executes for ax.tmux and no other backend. A request\n337|// naming any other backend refuses the failed local precondition,\n338|// never executes against the wrong backend.\n339|func checkLifecycleBackend(backendID string) error {\n340|\tif backendID != terminalbackend.BuiltinTmux {\n341|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"lifecycle backend\"}\n342|\t}\n343|\treturn nil\n344|}\n345|\n346|// checkBindingAgreement binds the create binding to its mutation\n347|// context: session, instance, backend, and generation must all agree.\n348|// Any disagreement refuses the failed local precondition: the binding\n349|// names another creation.\n350|func checkBindingAgreement(body CreateBody) error {\n351|\tif body.Binding.SessionID != body.Context.SessionID ||\n352|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalInstanceID != body.Context.TerminalInstanceID ||\n353|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalBackendID != body.Context.TerminalBackendID ||\n354|\t\tbody.Binding.BackendGeneration != body.Context.BackendGeneration {\n355|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"create binding agreement\"}\n356|\t}\n357|\treturn nil\n358|}\n359|\n360|// rowError normalizes a backend- or store-reported code against one\n361|// operation's allowed set: an in-row code propagates with its report,\n362|// while an outside-set code is itself refused as the protocol error —\n363|// the engine's CheckErrorAllowed arm, mirrored for the operations the\n364|// engine scope leaves out.\n365|func rowError(operation terminalbackend.Operation, err error) error {\n366|\tcode := backendErrorCode(err)\n367|\tif code == \"\" {\n368|\t\treturn err\n369|\t}\n370|\tif checkErr := terminalbackend.CheckErrorAllowed(string(operation), code); checkErr != nil {\n371|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"operation error vocabulary\"}\n372|\t}\n373|\treturn err\n374|}\n375|\n376|// formatTimestamp renders Now in the scalar timestamp grammar: UTC\n377|// RFC3339 with millisecond precision, always carrying the fractional\n378|// digits the grammar requires.\n379|func formatTimestamp(now time.Time) string {\n380|\treturn now.UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00\")\n381|}\n382|\n383|// executeCreate runs the full create body: closed-shape admission,\n384|// backend and transport gates, binding agreement, then the landed\n385|// engine with the tmux backend. The result echoes the carried binding\n386|// and, exactly when interactive, the unbound attach descriptor.\n387|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeCreate(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n388|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate}\n389|\tbody, err := parseCreateBody(req.Body)\n390|\tif err != nil {\n391|\t\treturn empty, err\n392|\t}\n393|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.Context.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n394|\t\treturn empty, err\n395|\t}\n396|\tif body.Transport == string(terminalbackend.TransportThirdPartyRelay) {\n397|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized, Detail: \"create relay transport\"}\n398|\t}\n399|\tif err := checkBindingAgreement(body); err != nil {\n400|\t\treturn empty, err\n401|\t}\n402|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.Context.SessionID, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n403|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationCreate\n404|\treqBackend.bootstrapID = body.BootstrapOperationID\n405|\treqBackend.bindingID = body.Binding.BindingID\n406|\treqBackend.bindingDoc = append([]byte(nil), body.BindingRaw...)\n407|\t_, completedBefore, err := lc.Receipts.Completed(body.Context.IdempotencyKey)\n408|\tif err != nil {\n409|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeProcessFailed, Detail: \"idempotency store failure\"}\n410|\t}\n411|\tresult, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteMutating(ctx, terminalbackend.OperationCreate, body.Context, terminstance.Params{\n412|\t\tBootstrapOperationID: body.BootstrapOperationID,\n413|\t\tInteractive:          body.Interactive,\n414|\t}, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n415|\toutcome := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate, Binding: &body.Binding}\n416|\tif result.OperationID != \"\" {\n417|\t\toutcome.Mutation = &result\n418|\t\tif err != nil {\n419|\t\t\tlc.recordFailure(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n420|\t\t} else {\n421|\t\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n422|\t\t}\n423|\t}\n424|\tif err != nil {\n425|\t\treturn outcome, err\n426|\t}\n427|\tif !completedBefore {\n428|\t\t// A fresh create success opens a new incarnation: prior\n429|\t\t// closure reports are superseded, so the new\n430|\t\t// incarnation's input starts open. Replays skip the\n431|\t\t// rotation — replaying an old success must not erase a\n432|\t\t// newer closure — and a failed rotation fails the\n433|\t\t// operation closed: the incarnation keeps its prior\n434|\t\t// value, prior proofs stay valid, and recovery is a\n435|\t\t// fresh create or restore.\n436|\t\tif err := lc.States.RecordIncarnation(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, body.Context.IdempotencyKey); err != nil {\n437|\t\t\treturn outcome, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeIntegrityFailure, Detail: \"create incarnation image\"}\n438|\t\t}\n439|\t}\n440|\tif body.Interactive {\n441|\t\tdescriptor := createDescriptor(socket, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n442|\t\toutcome.Descriptor = &descriptor\n443|\t}\n444|\treturn outcome, nil\n445|}\n446|\n447|// executeStatus runs one status query through the landed engine with\n448|// the tmux backend: no receipt, no side effects, no authorization.\n449|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeStatus(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n450|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus}\n451|\tbody, err := terminstance.ParseStatusBody(req.Body)\n452|\tif err != nil {\n453|\t\treturn empty, err\n454|\t}\n455|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n456|\t\treturn empty, err\n457|\t}\n458|\tinstance := body.TerminalInstanceID\n459|\tif !body.HasTerminalInstanceID {\n460|\t\tinstance = \"\"\n461|\t}\n462|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.SessionID, instance)\n463|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationStatus\n464|\treport, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteStatus(ctx, body, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n465|\tif err != nil {\n466|\t\treturn empty, err\n467|\t}\n468|\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus, Status: &report}, nil\n469|}\n470|\n471|// executeEngineOp runs one quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, or\n472|// request-stop body through the landed engine with the tmux backend,\n473|// adding the per-operation success members the engine's receipt scope\n474|// leaves out.\n475|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeEngineOp(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string, operation terminalbackend.Operation) (OpOutcome, error) {\n476|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: operation}\n477|\tmctx, params, err := terminstance.ParseOperationBody(string(operation), req.Body)\n478|\tif err != nil {\n479|\t\treturn empty, err\n480|\t}\n481|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n482|\t\treturn empty, err\n483|\t}\n484|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n485|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n486|\tswitch operation {\n487|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n488|\t\treqBackend.quiescence = params.QuiescenceGeneration\n489|\t\treqBackend.channel = BoundaryChannelPrefix + params.QuiescenceGeneration\n490|\t\treqBackend.proofKind = params.ProviderProofKind\n491|\t\twaitCtx, cancel := lc.boundWait(ctx, mctx, params.TimeoutMs)\n492|\t\tdefer cancel()\n493|\t\treqBackend.waitCtx = waitCtx\n494|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n495|\t\treqBackend.deadline = lc.lesserDeadline(mctx, params.GracefulTimeoutMs)\n496|\t}\n497|\tif operation == terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput {\n498|\t\t// Ordering contract, quiesce side: hold the barrier lock\n499|\t\t// across the engine input closure and the report commit\n500|\t\t// below, so no attach receipt commits between the tmux\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
