{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd5f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":1290,"recorded_at":1780531400002575,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c938-ff8c-7c40-9474-9fa08e488bb6"},"task_id":"01a0c938-ff8c-7c40-9474-9fa08e488bb6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c938-ff8c-7c40-9474-9fa08e488bb6","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-33-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('task-board.config.json'))\\ncmds=d.get('spawn',{}).get('worktree_isolation',{}).get('validation',{}).get('commands',[])\\nprint('count:',len(cmds))\\nfor i,c in enumerate(cmds): print(i+1,'::',c[:160])\\n\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 45; echo ===; git diff --stat HEAD -- task-board.config.json; echo ===; task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-1c28dz) { id checklist }' 2>&1 | head -c 3000\",\n  \"description\": \"Read validation commands and checklist\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"count: 30\\n1 :: test -z \\\"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\\\"\\n2 :: go build ./...\\n3 :: go vet ./...\\n4 :: go test ./... -count=1 -v\\n5 :: go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m\\n6 :: go test ./... -cover -count=1\\n7 :: go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n8 :: go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedOperationBodies$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n9 :: go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzNamespaceVocabulary$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n10 :: go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzUnknownFields$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n11 :: go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n12 :: go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n13 :: go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n14 :: go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n15 :: go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n16 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCheckArgv$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n17 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCheckMemberPath$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n18 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzIsEnvName$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n19 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzRedactCorpus$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n20 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzEscapeForTerminal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n21 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzRenderForTerminal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n22 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzGuardResolve$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n23 :: go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzDetectCaseCollision$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n24 :: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\n25 :: go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n26 :: GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...\\n27 :: GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...\\n28 :: git ls-files -z '*.json' | xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'\\n29 :: task-board validate\\n30 :: git diff --check\\n===\\n===\\n{\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Implement create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, and restore via structured commands\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate x entry census is committed as a table in the conformance matrix and mirrored in TRACEABILITY: every production entry that reaches each gate gets a named test plus an admitting narrowing row, or unreachable with a reason, or a stated bound with an owner; every gate implemented on two or more sides carries a row-count symmetry line\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The eight named operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) are each driven through a production entry by a named committed test, with the n-of-8 ratio and the call site stated per operation\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The exec and probe adapters that TASK-260830-35urbp declared as this leaf bound (its Dependencies had no production implementation) exist and are driven, and the server socket gets crash and idempotency evidence or an explicit purity bound\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The bounds 35urbp handed over are each dispositioned: B18 sun_path 104-byte limit on the derived socket path, B16 nested invocation from inside an AX pane (ambient collision, decide deliberately), B19/B20 SPEC 810-812 before-bind rejection of an unsafe root at the bind step, and the rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy foreground attach wiring if attach semantics land here rather than in g0pcnt\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Composing packages keep working, proven by an OUTCOME-keyed comparison over the complete importer set (not a name-keyed per-test diff of one package), with every input that moved across an admission or refusal arm named in the results\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every rule is driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere; any real-tmux test is separately gated and is never the only witness for an acceptance row, and the results state which rows have a real-tmux witness in addition to their deterministic one\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5399,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1350,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
