{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000db33","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":3060,"recorded_at":1780531400006115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c947-253a-7643-a75a-507691c223c5"},"task_id":"01a0c947-253a-7643-a75a-507691c223c5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c947-253a-7643-a75a-507691c223c5","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-66-1\",\n  \"command\": \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py N-attach-wait-deadline N-quiesce-detach-step N-quiesce-sendkeys-absent N-attach-barrier-recheck N-ordering-lock-attach N-ordering-lock-quiesce N-ordering-lock-boundary 2>&1 | tail -n 10; echo ===TERMBIND===; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-attach-peers-decode 2>&1 | tail -n 3\",\n  \"description\": \"Run wait row, repaired rows, termbind row\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"ok: N-quiesce-detach-step: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the lock-only barrier past the detach step; the lock step stays. Kill path: quiesce detaches nothing, at the helper and through the quiesce dispatch alike. [exit 1]\\nok: N-quiesce-sendkeys-absent: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly a provider-input step into the quiesce sequence; the lock/detach steps stay. Kill path: quiesce emits send-keys through the quiesce dispatch (the unscripted vector fails the run). [exit 1]\\nok: N-attach-barrier-recheck: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the authoritative barrier recheck (a post-quiescence attach commits its receipt); every other instance still revalidates. Kill path: the late attach succeeds with a writable receipt through the attach dispatch. [exit 1]\\nMISMATCH: N-ordering-lock-attach: SURVIVED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the attach side of the ordering lock (acquire-then-release: its critical section runs unlocked); every other instance still serializes. Kill path: the attach completes mid-commit inside the report write instead of blocking. [exit 0]\\nok: N-ordering-lock-quiesce: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the quiesce side of the ordering lock (acquire-then-release: its report commits unlocked); every other instance still serializes. Kill path: the attach completes mid-commit inside the report write instead of blocking. [exit 1]\\nok: N-ordering-lock-boundary: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the boundary side of the ordering lock (acquire-then-release: its report commits unlocked); every other instance still serializes. Kill path: the attach completes mid-commit inside the boundary report write instead of blocking. [exit 1]\\nok: N-attach-wait-deadline: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly waits expiring within the hour past the shared wait bound (every barrier and admission wait runs an hour long); cancellation still cancels. One shared site, four entries: the attach, quiesce, and boundary deadline tests redden (each blocks until its release) while the cancellation test stays green (attribution per test from the raw log). [exit 1]\\n===TERMBIND===\\nok: N-attach-peers-decode: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the undecodable peer past the census health arm as a skip (the corrupt receipt reads as no peer); every other census failure still errors. Kill path: the peer scan passes over the corrupt document instead of refusing the census. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2527,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 632,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
