{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e471","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":4243,"recorded_at":1780531400008481,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c957-1693-7752-81be-70ed7da06cd9"},"task_id":"01a0c957-1693-7752-81be-70ed7da06cd9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c957-1693-7752-81be-70ed7da06cd9","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-92-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '32,70p' /tmp/td8/matrix-rev7.md | cut -c1-120; echo ...; sed -n '110,142p' /tmp/td8/matrix-rev7.md | cut -c1-60; echo ...; sed -n '507,560p' /tmp/td8/matrix-rev7.md | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Survey matrix AC and bounds layout\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"## AC rows (34 of 34; mirrored from TRACEABILITY rows 59-92)\\n\\n| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\\n|---|--------|-----------|------|\\n| 59 | The exec adapter runs -S vectors with AX-owned argv only: exits and both streams report as data, TMUX/TMUX_TMPDIR\\n| 60 | The primitive vocabulary is exactly the ten tmux directives and the per-operation map covers exactly the eight li\\n| 61 | Every built vector is the fixed -S shape for its directive: the socket is pinned to the runtime leaf (ambient soc\\n| 62 | Dialing the socket reports live, stale, or unknown: refused and missing sockets are stale, a missing directory an\\n| 63 | The prober enforces dependencies, length, and custody before dialing: stale reports not-running, unknown errors, \\n| 64 | The broker prober reports the miss, admission reconciliation fails closed without a verifier, and the Production \\n| 65 | The spawner enforces length, custody, and the exec-site socket pin before spawning: a stale socket unlinks (hook-\\n| 66 | B18: the socket path refuses at or beyond the platform sun_path limit (104/108), counted in bytes. | CheckSocketL\\n| 67 | B19/B20: the socket verifies at exactly the runtime leaf, and the leaf custody delegates to the landed Verify wit\\n| 68 | B20: the runtime root verifies as a caller-owned directory unwritable by others through the landed no-follow open\\n| 69 | B20: every ancestor verifies as a non-symlink directory unwritable by others up the lexical chain; sticky directo\\n| 70 | B19: the socket path itself is bindable when absent and unlinkable when a socket; any other kind refuses so the s\\n| 71 | Create bodies are the closed six-member shape with the operation context, binding, bootstrap, entrypoint, transpo\\n| 72 | Attach bodies are the closed eleven-member shape: identity (session, instance, backend, versions, generation), cl\\n| 73 | Terminate bodies are the closed four-member shape with the stale lease, stale epoch, and evidence members. | pars\\n| 74 | Restore bodies are the closed four-member shape with the prior binding, checkpoint, and bootstrap members. | pars\\n| 75 | Execute admits all eight lifecycle operations through the dependency, vocabulary, scope, length, and custody pre-\\n| 76 | Every operation verifies the ax.tmux backend identity before dispatch; foreign backends refuse on all eight opera\\n| 77 | Out-of-row error codes normalize to the protocol error; in-row codes propagate with their report, on all eight ro\\n| 78 | Create runs the closed-shape admission, binding agreement, and relay refusal through the engine: interactive retu\\n| 79 | Attach returns the caller-executed vector with its descriptor and never execs an interactive attach: closed-shape\\n| 80 | Status classifies present, absent, and unknown observations against the AX-side memory: absence needs its stderr \\n| 81 | Quiesce, boundary, and stop run through the engine with their outcome members: quiesce locks then detaches with n\\n| 82 | Terminate-stale runs the key, capability, transition, authorization, generation, fencing, target, winner, and dea\\n| 83 | Restore runs the capability, prior-binding, and receipt-bound persist-plus-wrapper sequence, then returns the req\\n| 84 | The receipt discipline binds, replays, resumes, and completes under the idempotency key: tampered completions ref\\n| 85 | Deadlines are strict bounds at entry and before every effect: the on-deadline instant refuses, and the entry arm \\n| 86 | Generations validate at entry and recheck before every effect: drift between entry and effect refuses under the s\\n| 87 | The presented idempotency key re-derives from the request inputs on both receipt operations; an underived key ref\\n| 88 | The AX-side state memory records and looks up per-instance states with identity and value grammars: creating neve\\n| 89 | Every mutating operation is idempotent under retry and resumes uncertainty through status: second identical reque\\n| 90 | B16: lifecycle entries take no ambient input, so a nested invocation cannot collide through them; the child envir\\n| 91 | Terminate-stale decides over the landed fencing authorization with local target and winner bindings: the fencing \\n| 92 | The after-restore composition refreshes the mesh lease under the measured bound before deciding through the lande\\n\\n...\\n## Lifecycle operations (Section 4.C)\\n\\n8 of 8 operations driven through the production entry `Execu\\n(lifecycle.go:151), one dispatch arm each, plus the after-re\\ncomposition entry `ExecuteWrapperRestore` (wrapper.go:97):\\n\\n| Operation | Dispatch arm | Test |\\n|-----------|--------------|------|\\n| create | executeCreate (lifecycle.go:321) | TestExecuteCre\\n| attach | executeAttach (ops.go:66) | TestExecuteAttach, Te\\n| status | executeStatus (lifecycle.go:362) | TestExecuteSta\\n| quiesce | executeEngineOp (lifecycle.go:388) | TestExecute\\n| safe-boundary | executeEngineOp (lifecycle.go:388) | TestE\\n| stop | executeEngineOp (lifecycle.go:388) | TestExecuteSto\\n| terminate-stale | executeTerminate (ops.go:195) | TestExec\\n| restore | executeRestore (ops.go:345) | TestExecuteRestore\\n| after-restore | ExecuteWrapperRestore (wrapper.go:97) | Te\\n\\n| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\\n|---|--------|-----------|------|\\n| 78 | Create runs the closed-shape admission, binding agree\\n| 79 | Attach returns the caller-executed vector with its de\\n| 80 | Status classifies present, absent, and unknown observ\\n| 81 | Quiesce, boundary, and stop run through the engine wi\\n| 82 | Terminate-stale runs the key, capability, transition,\\n| 83 | Restore runs the capability, prior-binding, and recei\\n| 84 | The receipt discipline binds, replays, resumes, and c\\n| 85 | Deadlines are strict bounds at entry and before every\\n| 86 | Generations validate at entry and recheck before ever\\n| 87 | The presented idempotency key re-derives from the req\\n| 88 | The AX-side state memory records and looks up per-ins\\n| 92 | The after-restore composition refreshes the mesh leas\\n\\n...\\n## Bounds (mirrored B22-B43 plus carried dispositions)\\n\\n- B22 Singleton arms ship no narrowing mutant: admitting the\\n  singleton refused member is deleting the gate. Covered sites, each\\n  test-pinned in both directions where a fork exists: create relay\\n  transport (relay), descriptor presence fork (descpresence),\\n  attach admission nil (serveadmitnil), spawner runner nil\\n  (spawnnil), reconcile verifier nil (reconcilenil), states root\\n  empty (stateopen), persist/attach stores nil (storenil),\\n  failed-kill self-confirm (selfconfirm), and live-after-escalation\\n  (stoptimeout). The outcome-lookup empty-key arm left this bound:\\n  it narrows now (LookupOutcomeRefusesForgedKey /\\n  N-outcome-key-forged). Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\\n  grows a second refused member.\\n- B23 The landed status engine normalizes backend error details to\\n  \\\"status observation unknown\\\" (coded or not), so the cutrow and\\n  empty-panes narrowings measure at the helper entries while the\\n  dispatch legs pin the code. Owner: this leaf; retest if the\\n  engine stops normalizing.\\n- B24 The idempotency-store Completed read-failure arm is unstaged:\\n  no seam fails receipt reads (hooks fire on write paths only).\\n  Owner: hardening; stage with a read-failure seam to measure.\\n- B25 The Bind clean-miss sub-arm is unstageable: every Bind error\\n  the hooks stage leaves the committed file, so Lookup always finds\\n  it. The clean-found sub-arm is measured (N-bind-hook-found).\\n  Owner: hardening.\\n- B26 The attach effect-failure dispatch mapping is unstaged: no\\n  committed failure reaches it (the store replays identical\\n  receipts; conflicting receipts are untested at dispatch).\\n  Owner: hardening.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7580,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1895,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
