{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e785","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":4637,"recorded_at":1780531400009269,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"call_id":"call_01a0c958da3b75aaaa3d6068ad91e5a6","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-106-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '1,25p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev7 — attach effect-boundary enumeration; authkind evidence repair\\n\\n- P1+P2-A FIXED (same invariant, one enumeration): the attach admission-to-effect interval that rev6 closed for closure stayed open for generation and the request deadline. The post-lock boundary now revalidates every live fact — closure (existing recheck), server generation (new live `CurrentGeneration` read), request deadline (new live clock read, lock wait counted, kept distinct from authorization expiry) — while authorization expiry, transport, and input binding revalidate inside the commit call itself (`AttachStore.Attach` rechecks with the live clock and holds no wait before the no-replace install); transition, operation capability, and backend identity are pure checks over request-immutable members with nothing to revalidate. SPEC §4.C 1095 (\\\"rechecked immediately before each side effect\\\") is the pin. Regressions: rotation-during-lock-wait (channel-ordered, deterministic), admission-advances-clock-past-deadline with valid authorization, and the on-the-instant variant. Narrowings `N-attach-postlock-generation` / `N-attach-postlock-deadline` KILLED; sibling members (late instants) still refuse under the plants. Create/restore/stop never had the interval: the landed engine `runEffects` and this leaf's `runLifecycleEffects` recheck deadline+authorization+generation before every effect including the first, after any wait. Residual (B42 extended): a rotation between the recheck and the commit, in- or cross-process, in a wait-free window.\\n- P2-B CLOSED: `TestAttachAuthorizationMembersRefuseWithoutReceipt` (expiry/input/transport) asserts refusal AND receipt absence through `Execute(attach)`; `N-attach-input-escalation` (reviewer A3 shape on the landed gate, cross-package row) commits the receipt before the result binding refuses, so the killer's absence assertion reddens. Gate stays landed, no fork.\\n- P3 CLOSED: the two effect-loop authkind wirings are reclassified as supplementary `D-` rows (they refuse a permitted grant; they admit nothing), the entry authkind rows are converted to genuine no-bind narrowings (control-kind bodies bind under the plant and refuse only at the loop), and the shared loop side is measured by the genuinely admitting `N-lifecycle-loop-authorization` (pre-commit auth failures execute the first effect; post-commit still refuse), killing through both terminate and restore entries with per-entry attribution. Census: 256 measured of 5248 (generation EXA U1→M), symmetry lines recounted, battery 285/285 (279 N + 5 D + control).\\n- PROCESS: a new post-lock arm textually identical to the entry arm breaks the entry row's anchor count AND silently converts its kill into a reroute (the post-lock arm refuses the same verdict); the entry killer now asserts the admission never ran, pinning the refusal to the entry site. A shared-loop narrowing needs a killer per entry or one side is attribution-by-assertion.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev6 — attach/quiesce ordering contract; closure-authority escalation\\n\\n- P1-B FIXED: attach now revalidates the quiesce barrier under `Lifecycle.barrierMu` immediately before committing its writable client receipt, holding the lock through the receipt, the returned vector, and the advisory memory record; quiesce holds the same lock across engine closure plus report commit, boundary across its report commit only (the wait blocks on the wrapper signal). Contract: report commits and receipt commits are mutually exclusive, whichever lands first wins, no writable receipt commits after a durable closure report. Three committed tests: paused-admission late attach refuses, plus quiesce/boundary overlap tests that launch attach from inside the report write via the state crash seam and assert it blocks then refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck` and `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` (instance-scoped) all KILLED; symmetry attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1.\\n- P1-A ESCALATED (structural, not a fourth guard): a lost outcome-report write after committed engine closure still admits a fresh writable attach until retry heals the report, because admission consults the outcome proof alone and pending-vs-committed is unrepresentable there. Bound B43 names owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` and the scoped contract (completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed); row 79 now claims only the lost state-record write fails closed. Same window covers receipt/report crash and double loss. B42 states the in-process bound on the ordering lock (cross-process needs a lock file) and that the covered vector handoff ends at construction.\\n- P2-A CLOSED: three read-error arms now fail closed through `Execute(attach)` with tests plus reviewer-shaped narrowings — incarnation EISDIR-as-absence (`N-incarnation-read-absent`), outcomes ENOTDIR-as-absence (`N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`), outcome-file EISDIR skip via `.json`-symlink-to-dir (`N-outcome-file-read-skip`) — and the attach entry of the unsafe-root gate carries its own valid-body test plus `N-attach-entry-root-custody` (weakened attach is served, proving admission rather than rerouting).\\n- P2-B CLOSED: importer outcome corpus now covers 36/36 packages (198 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 7 declared candidate-only; 6/6 stable runs) with `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher/no-sink refusals, `sshtransport.New(zero)` invalid-snapshot refusal, and `crashgate.Lookup` known/unknown rows. Suite-verdict grid: 23,874 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 505 candidate-only additions, 0 fails.\\n- P3 CLOSED: Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates × 11 = 1540; total census 255 measured of 5248 with 186 bounds and 4807 unreachable, verified by script); row 72 lease-members prose corrected to the ownership-neutral authorization; README quiesce claim narrowed to report-committed refusal plus B43; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows: 277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control).\\n- PROCESS: an overlap test that consumes the attach result inside the hook then re-waits on the same channel hangs 10s under the lock-removal plant; putting the result back keeps the kill fast with two failure lines. Copying the outcome-grid driver into a tree breaks `go test ./...` via the specdoc no-product-command gate — run the driver, remove the directory, then run the suite.\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6559,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1640,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
