{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e7ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c930-3251-7961-8bb5-544ec0b1a36c"},"sequence":4657,"recorded_at":1780531400009309,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54c40bac-01d0-401d-8b14-649734ac40cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c959-0390-7572-a934-d7cc7dea0694"},"task_id":"01a0c959-0390-7572-a934-d7cc7dea0694","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c959-0390-7572-a934-d7cc7dea0694","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-22\n-\n-### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev7 — attach effect-boundary enumeration; authkind evidence repair\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-22\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed\n+\n+- P1-A FIXED (stop escalation + quiesce mid-sequence): the stop escalation revalidates the operation deadline, AX authorization over the live lease, and server generation after its poll before `kill-session` issues — a graceful timeout escalates, any other stale fact refuses without the kill — and the quiesce detach revalidates between the lock and detach commands. The two post-wait boundaries share one closure over the landed gates (same `CheckAuthorization` call, same generation read, row's own timeout code) with per-site skip narrowings; sibling paths probed with fact-mutation during their waits: create/restore single-command (rotation changes nothing), terminate tail (kill count stays one, refusal stands), boundary tail (post-signal command is the read-only rows probe). Graceful wait and operation deadline are distinct bounds. Narrowings: 3 shared arms + 2 per-site skips, all KILLED with per-test attribution; census effectrecheck stop 4 / quiesce 4.\n+- P2 FIXED (bounded waits, uniform barrier contract): the attach admission and barrier acquisition run under one wait context combining the operation deadline with caller cancellation — the entry bounds the wait itself (goroutine + select, late answers discarded), so even a non-cooperative adapter cannot hold the request past its deadline or commit late. Quiesce span and boundary report commit acquire through the same contract (row's own timeout code; boundary reports against its committed proof). Release-controlled tests prove refusal-before-release plus no-late-receipt; cancellation returns promptly. Narrowing `N-attach-wait-deadline` KILLED through all four deadline tests while the cancellation companion stays green.\n+- P1-B NARROWED (overlap fail-closed): this leaf has no liveness census, so a stored peer receipt reads as possibly live — a second client needs `multi_attach`, new input over an input peer needs `multiple_input_clients`, same-client retries exempt, unreadable peers fail closed. Over-strict by design (detached clients' receipts still trigger) until the liveness census lands; owner TASK-260922-vcx6yo, stated as B44. Narrowings `N-attach-overlap-multi` / `-input` KILLED with two-peer precision legs. The §4.C attach row claims only the fail-closed gate, never liveness.\n+- PROCESS: a new downstream bound shadows an upstream narrowing when it refuses the same member with the same verdict — the entry-deadline instant row is reclassified as survived-supplementary `D-attach-entry-deadline-shadowed` (enforced boundary measured at post-lock + wait), with deterministic fired-context pre-checks so the shadowing never races. An ordering-lock plant must skip the acquisition, not acquire-then-release (the wait alone preserves the order and the row survives). Census: 261 measured of 5376 (new rows effectrecheck/overlapmulti/overlapinput/waitbound), battery 293/293 + 41/41.\n+\n+## 2026-09-22\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev7 — attach effect-boundary enumeration; authkind evidence repair\n","final_result":true}}}
